acts on apples you certainly didn\'t know, yet!\";s:6:\"module\";s:0:\"\";s:16:\"extendToSubpages\";i:0;s:6:\"author\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"author_email\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"nav_title\";s:9:\"Fun facts\";s:8:\"nav_hide\";i:0;s:16:\"content_from_pid\";i:0;s:9:\"mount_pid\";i:0;s:12:\"mount_pid_ol\";i:0;s:8:\"l18n_cfg\";i:0;s:14:\"backend_layout\";s:19:\"pagets__Contentpage\";s:25:\"backend_layout_next_level\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"tsconfig_includes\";N;s:9:\"seo_title\";s:19:\"Fun Facts on Apples\";s:8:\"no_index\";i:0;s:9:\"no_follow\";i:0;s:8:\"og_title\";s:0:\"\";s:14:\"og_description\";N;s:8:\"og_image\";i:0;s:13:\"twitter_title\";s:0:\"\";s:19:\"twitter_description\";N;s:13:\"twitter_image\";i:0;s:12:\"twitter_card\";s:7:\"summary\";s:14:\"canonical_link\";s:0:\"\";s:16:\"sitemap_priority\";s:3:\"0.5\";s:18:\"sitemap_changefreq\";s:0:\"\";s:10:\"categories\";i:0;s:15:\"infotext_header\";s:43:\"More information about the \"Fun facts\" page\";s:8:\"infotext\";s:900:\"<p>This page is a regular Content page type, and is divided into two sections: <strong>Stage content</strong>&nbsp;(at the top of the page) and <strong>Main content</strong>&nbsp;(the body of the page).</p>\r\n<p>The different sections allow different content types to be displayed. Having pre-defined sections lets you restrict what content can be included meaning editors can \"build\" new pages without having to worry about the design. For example,&nbsp;the Content page type allows a Keyvisual element to be inserted at the top of the page (in the Stage Content section), but not anywhere else on the page (the Main Content section), because that would not suit the design of the website.</p>\r\n<p>This page includes a content element that is only visible to users who have logged in to the frontend. This is done in the properties of the content element on the <strong>Access </strong>tab.&nbsp;</p>\";s:21:\"tx_schema_webpagetype\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"link\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"subpages\";a:0:{}s:11:\"hasSubpages\";b:0;}i:1;a:80:{s