ch\":\"\",\"tsconfig_includes\":\"\",\"hidden\":\"\",\"nav_hide\":\"\",\"fe_group\":\"\",\"editlock\":\"\",\"infotext_header\":\"\",\"infotext\":\"\",\"backend_layout\":\"\"}\";s:9:\"t3ver_oid\";i:0;s:10:\"t3ver_wsid\";i:0;s:11:\"t3ver_state\";i:0;s:11:\"t3ver_stage\";i:0;s:12:\"perms_userid\";i:1;s:13:\"perms_groupid\";i:1;s:10:\"perms_user\";i:31;s:11:\"perms_group\";i:31;s:15:\"perms_everybody\";i:1;s:5:\"title\";s:15:\"Kinds of apples\";s:4:\"slug\";s:15:\"/kind-of-apples\";s:7:\"doktype\";i:13;s:8:\"TSconfig\";N;s:11:\"is_siteroot\";i:0;s:13:\"php_tree_stop\";i:0;s:8:\"shortcut\";i:0;s:13:\"shortcut_mode\";i:0;s:8:\"subtitle\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"layout\";i:0;s:6:\"target\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"media\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"lastUpdated\";i:0;s:8:\"keywords\";s:29:\"TYPO3, CMS, Open Source, Demo\";s:13:\"cache_timeout\";i:0;s:10:\"cache_tags\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"newUntil\";i:0;s:11:\"description\";s:89:\"Find out more about the most popular kinds of apples worldwide on our TYPO3 Demo Project.\";s:9:\"no_search\";i:0;s:15:\"SYS_LASTCHANGED\";i:1643190720;s:8:\"abstract\";s:89:\"Find out more about the most popular kinds of apples worldwide on our TYPO3 Demo Project.\";s:6:\"module\";s:0:\"\";s:16:\"extendToSubpages\";i:0;s:6:\"author\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"author_email\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"nav_title\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"nav_hide\";i:0;s:16:\"content_from_pid\";i:0;s:9:\"mount_pid\";i:0;s:12:\"mount_pid_ol\";i:0;s:8:\"l18n_cfg\";i:0;s:14:\"backend_layout\";s:20:\"pagets__Overviewpage\";s:25:\"backend_layout_next_level\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"tsconfig_includes\";N;s:9:\"seo_title\";s:36:\"Kinds of apples - TYPO3 Demo Project\";s:8:\"no_index\";i:0;s:9:\"no_follow\";i:0;s:8:\"og_title\";s:0:\"\";s:14:\"og_description\";N;s:8:\"og_image\";s:0:\"\";s:13:\"twitter_title\";s:0:\"\";s:19:\"twitter_description\";N;s:13:\"twitter_image\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"twitter_card\";s:7:\"summary\";s:14:\"canonical_link\";s:0:\"\";s:16:\"sitemap_priority\";s:3:\"0.5\";s:18:\"sitemap_changefreq\";s:0:\"\";s:10:\"categories\";s:0:\"\";s:15:\"infotext_header\";s:53:\"More information about the â€œKinds of applesâ€ page\";s:8:\"infotext\";s:1265:\"<p>This page, and the <a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=4\" target=\"_top\">\"Recipes\" page</a> are both Overview page types.<br /> Overview pages are&nbsp;divided into three sections:</p>\r\n<ul> 	<li>Stage content</li> 	<li>Main content</li> 	<li>Teaser content</li> </ul>\r\n<p>You will notice that in the Stage content and the Teaser content section,&nbsp;you can only insert a certain content type. This&nbsp;helps editors \"build\" pages without having to worry about the frontend design.</p>\r\n<p>In the Teaser content section, you can insert the content type <strong>Teaser list of all subpages</strong>. This&nbsp;is a very practical content type that makes it easy for editors to display teasers of certain pages (in this case kinds of apples or recipes). All information for the teasers (like title, teaser text and teaser image) are edited on the recipe or apple page itself. For example,&nbsp;to change the teaser image for a certain recipe, you need to go into the page properties of that particular recipe and edit the data there.</p>\r\n<p>This way you can make sure that all data&nbsp;will be changed on every page immediately.&nbsp;It also saves you time because&nbsp;you don\'t have to find every single page the teaser is used on.</p>\";s:21:\"tx_schema_webpagetype\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"link\";s:0:\"\";}i:0;a:78:{s:3:\"uid\";i:1;s:3:\"pid\";i:0;s:6:\"tstamp\";i:1666592511;s:6:\"crdate\";i:1601645180;s:7:\"deleted\";i:0;s:6:\"hidden\";i:0;s:9:\"starttime\";i:0;s:7:\"endtime\";i:0;s:8:\"fe_group\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"sorting\";i:512;s:14:\"rowDescription\";N;s:8:\"editlock\";i:0;s:16:\"sys_language_uid\";i:0;s:11:\"l10n_parent\";i:0;s:11:\"l10n_source\";i:0;s:10:\"l10n_state\";N;s:15:\"l10n_diffsource\";s:580:\"{\"doktype\":\"\",\"title\":\"\",\"slug\":\"\",\"nav_title\":\"\",\"seo_title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"no_index\":\"\",\"no_follow\":\"\",\"canonical_link\":\"\",\"tx_schema_webpagetype\":\"\",\"sitemap_changefreq\":\"\",\"sitemap_priority\":\"\",\"og_title\":\"\",\"og_description\":\"\",\"og_image\":\"\",\"twitter_title\":\"\",\"twitter_description\":\"\",\"twitter_image\":\"\",\"twitter_card\":\"\",\"abstract\":\"\",\"keywords\":\"\",\"target\":\"\",\"cache_tags\":\"\",\"is_siteroot\":\"\",\"no_search\":\"\",\"no_search_sub_entries\":\"\",\"tsconfig_includes\":\"\",\"hidden\":\"\",\"nav_hide\":\"\",\"fe_group\":\"\",\"editlock\":\"\",\"infotext_header\":\"\",\"infotext\":\"\",\"backend_layout\":\"\"}\";s:9:\"t3ver_oid\";i:0;s:10:\"t3ver_wsid\";i:0;s:11:\"t3ver_state\";i:0;s:11:\"t3ver_stage\";i:0;s:12:\"perms_userid\";i:1;s:13:\"perms_groupid\";i:1;s:10:\"perms_user\";i:31;s:11:\"perms_group\";i:31;s:15:\"perms_everybody\";i:1;s:5:\"title\";s:15:\"TYPO3 Demo Site\";s:4:\"slug\";s:1:\"/\";s:7:\"doktype\";i:10;s:8:\"TSconfig\";N;s:11:\"is_siteroot\";i:1;s:13:\"php_tree_stop\";i:0;s:8:\"shortcut\";i:0;s:13:\"shortcut_mode\";i:0;s:8:\"subtitle\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"layout\";i:0;s:6:\"target\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"media\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"lastUpdated\";i:0;s:8:\"keywords\";s:47:\"TYPO3, CMS, Demo, Open Source, Experience TYPO3\";s:13:\"cache_timeout\";i:0;s:10:\"cache_tags\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"newUntil\";i:0;s:11:\"description\";s:132:\"Get an insight on how the CMS TYPO3 works, log in to the backend, edit and delete content and experience TYPO3â€™s amazing features.\";s:9:\"no_search\";i:0;s:15:\"SYS_LASTCHANGED\";i:1666592511;s:8:\"abstract\";s:130:\"Get an insight on how the CMS TYPO3 works, log in to the backend, edit and delete content and experience TYPO3\'s amazing features.\";s:6:\"module\";s:0:\"\";s:16:\"extendToSubpages\";i:0;s:6:\"author\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"author_email\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"nav_title\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"nav_hide\";i:0;s:16:\"content_from_pid\";i:0;s:9:\"mount_pid\";i:0;s:12:\"mount_pid_ol\";i:0;s:8:\"l18n_cfg\";i:0;s:14:\"backend_layout\";s:17:\"pagets__Startpage\";s:25:\"backend_layout_next_level\";s:19:\"pagets__Contentpage\";s:17:\"tsconfig_includes\";N;s:9:\"seo_title\";s:18:\"TYPO3 Demo Project\";s:8:\"no_index\";i:0;s:9:\"no_follow\";i:0;s:8:\"og_title\";s:0:\"\";s:14:\"og_description\";N;s:8:\"og_image\";s:0:\"\";s:13:\"twitter_title\";s:0:\"\";s:19:\"twitter_description\";N;s:13:\"twitter_image\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"twitter_card\";s:7:\"summary\";s:14:\"canonical_link\";s:0:\"\";s:16:\"sitemap_priority\";s:3:\"0.5\";s:18:\"sitemap_changefreq\";s:0:\"\";s:10:\"categories\";s:0:\"\";s:15:\"infotext_header\";s:35:\"More information about this project\";s:8:\"infotext\";s:1887:\"<p>The workspace of the TYPO3 backend is divided into three sections:</p>\r\n<ol> 	<li>The module menu on the left of the screen</li> 	<li>The page tree - its structure represents the sitemap of your website</li> 	<li>The content area where you can edit pages and content elements</li> </ol>\r\n<p>This project uses several different page types:</p>\r\n<ul> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=1\" target=\"_top\">Start page</a></li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=17\" target=\"_top\">Apple page</a> (specifically configured for this project)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=39\" target=\"_top\">Recipe page</a> (specifically configured for this project)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=4\" target=\"_top\">Overview page</a> (specifically configured for this project)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=96\" target=\"_top\">Content page</a>&nbsp;(specifically configured for this project)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=7\" target=\"_top\">Shortcut</a> (default TYPO3 page type)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=12\" target=\"_top\">Link to external URLs</a> (default TYPO3 page type)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=11\" target=\"_top\">Folder</a> (default TYPO3 page type)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=52\" target=\"_top\">Content page with restricted access for frontend users</a> (default TYPO3 page type;&nbsp;this&nbsp;is for pages that are only shown to users who are logged in to the frontend)</li> </ul>\r\n<p>These different page types have pre-defined content sections that provide a guideline for structuring content on the page, making it easy for editors to create and \"build\" pages.</p>\";s:21:\"tx_schema_webpagetype\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"link\";s:0:\"\";}}'),
