?id=4\" target=\"_top\">Overview page</a> (specifically configured for this project)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=96\" target=\"_top\">Content page</a>&nbsp;(specifically configured for this project)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=7\" target=\"_top\">Shortcut</a> (default TYPO3 page type)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=12\" target=\"_top\">Link to external URLs</a> (default TYPO3 page type)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=11\" target=\"_top\">Folder</a> (default TYPO3 page type)</li> 	<li><a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=52\" target=\"_top\">Content page with restricted access for frontend users</a> (default TYPO3 page type;&nbsp;this&nbsp;is for pages that are only shown to users who are logged in to the frontend)</li> </ul>\r\n<p>These different page types have pre-defined content sections that provide a guideline for structuring content on the page, making it easy for editors to create and \"build\" pages.</p>\";s:21:\"tx_schema_webpagetype\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"link\";s:0:\"\";}}'),
