(54,4,1624530750,1603203741,0,0,0,0,'',2176,NULL,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"description\":null}',0,0,0,0,1,1,31,31,1,'Apple Cinnamon Tea','/recipes/apple-cinnamon-tea',12,NULL,0,0,0,0,'',0,'',1,0,'Apple Cinnamon Tea, TYPO3, CMS, Open Source, Demo',0,'',0,'Looking for a great recipe for an Apple Cinnamon Tea? Try the one we published on the TYPO3 Demo project!',0,1643119157,'A nice cup of tea is always a good idea for cold days!','',0,'','','',0,0,0,0,0,'pagets__Recipepage','',NULL,'Apple Cinnamon Tea - TYPO3 Demo Project',0,0,'',NULL,0,'',NULL,0,'summary','',0.5,'',0,'For more information on recipe pages check out the â€œApple pieâ€ page',NULL,'',''),
(56,1,1643191257,1603288202,0,0,0,0,'',2944,NULL,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"doktype\":\"\",\"title\":\"\",\"slug\":\"\",\"nav_title\":\"\",\"seo_title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"no_index\":\"\",\"no_follow\":\"\",\"canonical_link\":\"\",\"tx_schema_webpagetype\":\"\",\"sitemap_changefreq\":\"\",\"sitemap_priority\":\"\",\"og_title\":\"\",\"og_description\":\"\",\"og_image\":\"\",\"twitter_title\":\"\",\"twitter_description\":\"\",\"twitter_image\":\"\",\"twitter_card\":\"\",\"abstract\":\"\",\"keywords\":\"\",\"target\":\"\",\"cache_tags\":\"\",\"is_siteroot\":\"\",\"no_search\":\"\",\"media\":\"\",\"tsconfig_includes\":\"\",\"hidden\":\"\",\"nav_hide\":\"\",\"fe_group\":\"\",\"editlock\":\"\",\"infotext_header\":\"\",\"infotext\":\"\",\"backend_layout\":\"\"}',0,0,0,0,1,1,31,31,1,'FAQ','/faq',15,NULL,0,0,0,0,'',0,'',0,0,'FAQ, TYPO3, CMS, Open Source, Demo',0,'faq',0,'Frequently asked questions about apples - you will find some answers on the TYPO3 demo project!',0,1643192179,'Frequently asked questions about apples - you will find some answers on the TYPO3 demo project!','',0,'','','',0,0,0,0,0,'pagets__Faqpage','',NULL,'FAQ on Apples - Answered on the TYPO3 Demo project',0,0,'',NULL,0,'',NULL,0,'summary','',0.5,'',0,'More information about the â€œFAQâ€ page','<p>The FAQ page is a regular content page that is divided into two sections: the stage and main content.</p>\r\n<p>The FAQ is a <a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/faq\" target=\"_top\">custom-built backend module</a>. You can see it in the module menu on the left of the screen.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>When adding content to this page, we went to the <strong>Special elements</strong> tab to insert the \'FAQ Listing\' content type. This inserts all FAQs from the <a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/faq\" target=\"_top\">FAQ module</a>. The questions will disappear from the page&nbsp;as soon as they are&nbsp;deleted or hidden, and will display on the page as soon as they are unhidden, or a new question is created.</p>\r\n<p>That makes it easy for editors because they don\'t need to worry about manually adjusting questions whenever something changes in the FAQ area.</p>','',''),
(57,1,1607423922,1603789107,0,0,0,0,'',256,NULL,0,1,2,2,'{\"starttime\":\"parent\",\"endtime\":\"parent\",\"nav_hide\":\"parent\",\"url\":\"parent\",\"lastUpdated\":\"parent\",\"newUntil\":\"parent\",\"no_search\":\"parent\",\"shortcut\":\"parent\",\"shortcut_mode\":\"parent\",\"content_from_pid\":\"parent\",\"author\":\"parent\",\"author_email\":\"parent\",\"media\":\"parent\",\"og_image\":\"parent\",\"twitter_image\":\"parent\"}','{\"doktype\":1,\"title\":\"Fun facts\",\"slug\":\"\\/fun-facts\",\"nav_title\":\"\",\"subtitle\":\"\",\"seo_title\":\"Fun Facts on Apples\",\"description\":\"Find out some fun facts on apples you certainly didn\'t know, yet!\",\"canonical_link\":\"\",\"sitemap_changefreq\":\"\",\"sitemap_priority\":\"0.5\",\"og_title\":\"\",\"og_description\":null,\"twitter_title\":\"\",\"twitter_description\":null,\"twitter_card\":\"summary\",\"abstract\":\"Find out some fun facts on apples you certainly didn\'t know, yet!\",\"keywords\":\"Fun Facts, Apples, TYPO3\",\"hidden\":0,\"categories\":0,\"rowDescription\":null,\"TSconfig\":null,\"php_tree_stop\":0,\"editlock\":0,\"layout\":0,\"fe_group\":\"\",\"extendToSubpages\":0,\"target\":\"\",\"cache_timeout\":0,\"cache_tags\":\"\",\"mount_pid\":0,\"is_siteroot\":0,\"mount_pid_ol\":0,\"module\":\"\",\"fe_login_mode\":0,\"l18n_cfg\":0,\"backend_layout\":\"pagets__Contentpage\",\"backend_layout_next_level\":\"\",\"tsconfig_includes\":null,\"no_index\":0,\"no_follow\":0,\"starttime\":0,\"endtime\":0,\"nav_hide\":0,\"url\":\"\",\"lastUpdated\":0,\"newUntil\":0,\"no_search\":0,\"shortcut\":0,\"shortcut_mode\":0,\"content_from_pid\":0,\"author\":\"\",\"author_email\":\"\",\"media\":0,\"og_image\":0,\"twitter_image\":0,\"infotext_header\":\"More information about the \\\"Fun facts\\\" page\",\"infotext\":\"<p>This page is a regular Content page type, and is divided into two sections: <strong>Stage content<\\/strong>&nbsp;(at the top of the page) and <strong>Main content<\\/strong>&nbsp;(the body of the page).<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>The different sections allow different content types to be displayed. Having pre-defined sections lets you restrict what content can be included meaning editors can \\\"build\\\" new pages without having to worry about the design. For example,&nbsp;the Content page type allows a Keyvisual element to be inserted at the top of the page (in the Stage Content section), but not anywhere else on the page (the Main Content section), because that would not suit the design of the website.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>This page includes a content element that is only visible to users who have logged in to the frontend. This is done in the properties of the content element on the <strong>Access <\\/strong>tab.&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}',0,0,0,0,1,1,31,31,1,'Fun Facts','/fun-facts',1,NULL,0,0,0,0,'',0,'',0,0,'Fun Facts, Ã„pfel, TYPO3',0,'',0,'Hier findest Du ein paar Fakten Ã¼ber Ã„pfel, die wahrscheinlich neu fÃ¼r Dich sind!',0,1643123090,'Hier findest Du ein paar Fakten Ã¼ber Ã„pfel, die wahrscheinlich neu fÃ¼r Dich sind!','',0,'','','',0,0,0,0,0,'pagets__Contentpage','','','Fun Facts Ã¼ber Ã„pfel',0,0,'',NULL,0,'',NULL,0,'summary','',0.5,'',0,'More information about the \"Fun facts\" page','<p>This page is a regular Content page type, and is divided into two sections: <strong>Stage content</strong>&nbsp;(at the top of the page) and <strong>Main content</strong>&nbsp;(the body of the page).</p>\r\n<p>The different sections allow different content types to be displayed. Having pre-defined sections lets you restrict what content can be included meaning editors can \"build\" new pages without having to worry about the design. For example,&nbsp;the Content page type allows a Keyvisual element to be inserted at the top of the page (in the Stage Content section), but not anywhere else on the page (the Main Content section), because that would not suit the design of the website.</p>\r\n<p>This page includes a content element that is only visible to users who have logged in to the frontend. This is done in the properties of the content element on the <strong>Access </strong>tab.&nbsp;</p>','',''),
(60,1,1643190720,1606731043,0,0,0,0,'',2048,NULL,0,1,3,3,'{\"starttime\":\"parent\",\"endtime\":\"parent\",\"nav_hide\":\"parent\",\"url\":\"parent\",\"lastUpdated\":\"parent\",\"newUntil\":\"parent\",\"no_search\":\"parent\",\"shortcut\":\"parent\",\"shortcut_mode\":\"parent\",\"content_from_pid\":\"parent\",\"author\":\"parent\",\"author_email\":\"parent\",\"media\":\"parent\",\"og_image\":\"parent\",\"twitter_image\":\"parent\",\"tx_schema_webpagetype\":\"parent\"}','{\"doktype\":13,\"title\":\"Kinds of apples\",\"slug\":\"\\/kind-of-apples\",\"nav_title\":\"\",\"seo_title\":\"Kinds of apples - TYPO3 Demo Project\",\"description\":\"Find out more about the most popular kinds of apples worldwide on our TYPO3 Demo Project.\",\"canonical_link\":\"\",\"sitemap_changefreq\":\"\",\"sitemap_priority\":\"0.5\",\"og_title\":\"\",\"og_description\":null,\"twitter_title\":\"\",\"twitter_description\":null,\"twitter_card\":\"summary\",\"abstract\":\"Find out more about the most popular kinds of apples worldwide on our TYPO3 Demo Project.\",\"keywords\":\"TYPO3, CMS, Open Source, Demo\",\"hidden\":0,\"TSconfig\":\"\",\"php_tree_stop\":\"0\",\"editlock\":\"0\",\"layout\":\"0\",\"fe_group\":\"\",\"extendToSubpages\":\"0\",\"target\":\"\",\"cache_timeout\":\"0\",\"cache_tags\":\"\",\"mount_pid\":\"0\",\"is_siteroot\":\"0\",\"mount_pid_ol\":\"0\",\"module\":\"\",\"fe_login_mode\":\"0\",\"l18n_cfg\":\"0\",\"backend_layout\":\"pagets__Overviewpage\",\"backend_layout_next_level\":\"\",\"tsconfig_includes\":\"\",\"no_index\":\"0\",\"no_follow\":\"0\",\"infotext_header\":\"More information about the \\u201cKinds of apples\\u201d page\",\"infotext\":\"<p>This page, and the <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/demo.typo3.org\\/typo3\\/module\\/web\\/layout?id=4\\\" target=\\\"_top\\\">\\\"Recipes\\\" page<\\/a> are both Overview page types.<br \\/> Overview pages are&nbsp;divided into three sections:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul> \\t<li>Stage content<\\/li> \\t<li>Main content<\\/li> \\t<li>Teaser content<\\/li> <\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>You will notice that in the Stage content and the Teaser content section,&nbsp;you can only insert a certain content type. This&nbsp;helps editors \\\"build\\\" pages without having to worry about the frontend design.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>In the Teaser content section, you can insert the content type <strong>Teaser list of all subpages<\\/strong>. This&nbsp;is a very practical content type that makes it easy for editors to display teasers of certain pages (in this case kinds of apples or recipes). All information for the teasers (like title, teaser text and teaser image) are edited on the recipe or apple page itself. For example,&nbsp;to change the teaser image for a certain recipe, you need to go into the page properties of that particular recipe and edit the data there.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>This way you can make sure that all data&nbsp;will be changed on every page immediately.&nbsp;It also saves you time because&nbsp;you don\'t have to find every single page the teaser is used on.<\\/p>\",\"starttime\":\"0\",\"endtime\":\"0\",\"nav_hide\":\"0\",\"url\":\"\",\"lastUpdated\":\"0\",\"newUntil\":\"0\",\"no_search\":\"0\",\"shortcut\":\"0\",\"shortcut_mode\":\"0\",\"content_from_pid\":\"0\",\"author\":\"\",\"author_email\":\"\",\"media\":\"0\",\"og_image\":\"0\",\"twitter_image\":\"0\",\"tx_schema_webpagetype\":\"\"}',0,0,0,0,1,1,31,31,1,'Apfelsorten','/apfelsorten',13,NULL,0,0,0,0,'',0,'',0,0,'TYPO3, CMS, Open Source, Demo',0,'',0,'Lerne mehr Ã¼ber die beliebtesten Apfelsorten weltweit in unserem TYPO3 Demoprojekt.',0,1643190720,'Lerne mehr Ã¼ber die beliebtesten Apfelsorten weltweit in unserem TYPO3 Demoprojekt.','',0,'','','',0,0,0,0,0,'pagets__Overviewpage','','','Apfelsorten - TYPO3 Demo Project',0,0,'',NULL,0,'',NULL,0,'summary','',0.5,'',0,'More information about the â€œKinds of applesâ€ page','<p>This page, and the <a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/layout?id=4\" target=\"_top\">\"Recipes\" page</a> are both Overview page types.<br /> Overview pages are&nbsp;divided into three sections:</p>\r\n<ul> 	<li>Stage content</li> 	<li>Main content</li> 	<li>Teaser content</li> </ul>\r\n<p>You will notice that in the Stage content and the Teaser content section,&nbsp;you can only insert a certain content type. This&nbsp;helps editors \"build\" pages without having to worry about the frontend design.</p>\r\n<p>In the Teaser content section, you can insert the content type <strong>Teaser list of all subpages</strong>. This&nbsp;is a very practical content type that makes it easy for editors to display teasers of certain pages (in this case kinds of apples or recipes). All information for the teasers (like title, teaser text and teaser image) are edited on the recipe or apple page itself. For example,&nbsp;to change the teaser image for a certain recipe, you need to go into the page properties of that particular recipe and edit the data there.</p>\r\n<p>This way you can make sure that all data&nbsp;will be changed on every page immediately.&nbsp;It also saves you time because&nbsp;you don\'t have to find every single page the teaser is used on.</p>','',''),
