INSERT INTO `tt_content` VALUES
(1,'',1,1643119157,1601915381,0,0,0,0,'',768,1,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":\"\",\"colPos\":\"\",\"header\":\"\",\"bodytext\":\"\",\"link\":\"\",\"linklabel\":\"\",\"sys_language_uid\":\"\",\"hidden\":\"\",\"starttime\":\"\",\"endtime\":\"\",\"fe_group\":\"\",\"editlock\":\"\",\"rowDescription\":\"\"}',0,0,0,0,'footerinfo','Take a look at the backend','','You\'re thinking about choosing TYPO3 as a CMS for your next project and would like to find out more about what\'s amazing about this Open Source CMS? \r\nYou\'re welcome to login to the backend, edit and delete whatever you like and fall in love with TYPO3!',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'0','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,21,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(13,'',29,1606192281,1602491621,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"image\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'contentstage','Oops, we can\'t find this page! This link might be rotten or someone must have eaten it up!','',NULL,0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(18,'',17,1606733193,1602511935,0,0,0,0,'',1036,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"bodytext\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The Belle de Boskoop is a good choice for many recipes. Due to its&nbsp;high acidity it works well for apple sauce,&nbsp;apple pancakes, apple pies or baked apples.</p>\r\n<p>It is also widely used for apple juice, apple wine and fruit brandy.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> If you tend to have an allergic reaction&nbsp;to some apples, the Belle de Boskoop is an ideal choice&nbsp;due to its low allergen levels.</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(20,'',17,1606733207,1602517053,0,0,0,0,'',1152,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The apple grows very well in France\'s Normandy and ripens by the end of September until mid-October. Storing the apple after harvest (until March of the following year) should be no problem at all!</p>\r\n<p>The tree with its strongly growing and overhanging treetop grows best on heavy, moist and preferably calcareous&nbsp;soil.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> The trees have proven to be very fire-resistant!</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,1,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(27,'',18,1606733344,1602583647,0,0,0,0,'',768,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"bodytext\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>Braeburn apple trees, compared to other apple trees, are rather easy to cultivate. The fruit requires a long vegetation period, though, which is why it grows best in warm climates. The apples are mostly cultivated commercially in Chile, the USA and Southern Europe.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Braeburn apples are available from October to April in the northern hemisphere, and even young trees will be able to provide a good harvest.</p>\r\n<p>Fruit growers love the cultivar as it can be stored easily in chilly places and is&nbsp;able to be preserved by short, medium or long-term storage&nbsp;(3-4 months at 0Â°C and for 8-10 months).</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(28,'',18,1606733331,1602584009,0,0,0,0,'',48,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The apple is ideal for a variety of recipes like fruit salads, apple sauce and apple juice.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> If you tend to have an allergic reaction&nbsp;to some apples, the Braeburn is not a good choice for you.</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(31,'',19,1606617880,1602599890,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>In terms of pest and disease susceptibility, Elstar apples are rather resistant&nbsp;compared to other cultivars. It is, however, susceptible to apple scab, mildew and collar rot.</p>\r\n<p>The apple grows especially well when planted in cooler climates, and only takes a short period of time for growth so it is usually edible right after harvest.</p>\r\n<p>Harvest happens during the month of September and apples can be stored until the end of November in cool places (or even through to February if stored in a controlled atmosphere).</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,17,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,1,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(34,'',19,1606617740,1602600824,0,0,0,0,'',32,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>It is ideal for cooking and used for apple sauce very often. Due to its sweet flavour it is mostly used for desserts.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> If you tend to have an allergic reaction&nbsp;to some apples, you should avoid an Elstar apple.</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(36,'',19,1606831223,1602669438,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,'45,39,41,54',2,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(38,'',39,1606615355,1602669715,0,0,0,0,'',512,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'ingredients','Ingredients','','<table> 	<thead> 		<tr> 			<th scope=\"col\">Quantity</th> 			<th scope=\"col\">Product</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2 cup</td> 			<td>Sugar</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2 cup</td> 			<td>Firmly packed brown sugar</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>3 tbsp</td> 			<td>All-purpose flour</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 tsp</td> 			<td>Ground cinnamon</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/4 tsp</td> 			<td>Ground ginger</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/4 tsp</td> 			<td>Ground nutmeg</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>6-7 cups</td> 			<td>Thinly sliced peeled tart apples</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 tbsp</td> 			<td>Lemon juice</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td></td> 			<td>Pastry for double-crust pie</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 tbsp</td> 			<td>Butter</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1</td> 			<td>Large egg white</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td></td> 			<td>Additional sugar</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(39,'',39,1607344639,1602670118,0,0,0,0,'',768,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Directions','','<p><strong>Step 1</strong></p>\r\n<p>Combine the sugars, flour and spices in a small bowl and set aside. In a larger bowl, toss apples with lemon juice and add the sugar mixture; toss to coat.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong></p>\r\n<p>Line a 9-inch&nbsp;pie plate with bottom crust and trim even with edge. Fill the plate with apple mixture and dot with butter. Roll the remaining crust to fit the top of the pie and place it over the filling. Trim, seal and flute the edges and cut slits in the crust.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 3</strong></p>\r\n<p>Beat the egg white until it turns foamy; brush the egg white over the crust and sprinkle it with sugar. Cover the edges loosely with foil.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 4</strong></p>\r\n<p>Bake the cake at 375Â°F&nbsp;for 25 minutes. Remove the foil and bake until the crust is golden brown and the&nbsp;filling is bubbly (about 20-25 minutes). Cool the cake on a wire rack.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Recipe from&nbsp;https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/apple-pie/</sup></p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(40,'',39,1602673001,1602670230,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Learn more about apples','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,'24,18,23,25',2,'','',0,3,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(42,'',41,1602671344,1602671261,0,0,0,0,'',512,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'ingredients','Ingredients','','<table> 	<thead> 		<tr> 			<th scope=\"col\">Quantity</th> 			<th scope=\"col\">Product</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td>4 cups</td> 			<td>Sugar</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>2 cups</td> 			<td>Water</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>4 pounds</td> 			<td>Apples, sliced</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 liter</td> 			<td>Brandy</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>3</td> 			<td>Whole cloves</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1</td> 			<td>cinnamon stick (3 inches)</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td></td> 			<td>Additional whole cloves and cinnamon sticks</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(43,'',41,1607344729,1602671382,0,0,0,0,'',768,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Directions','','<p><strong>Step 1</strong></p>\r\n<p>Combine the&nbsp;sugar and water in a large saucepan and bring all of it to a boil; cook and stir the mixture until the sugar is dissolved. Remove the mixture&nbsp;from the heat.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong></p>\r\n<p>Place the apples in a large glass or plastic container; add the sugar mixture, brandy, cloves and cinnamon stick. Cover the mixture and let it stand at room temperature for at least two weeks, stirring it once a week.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 3</strong></p>\r\n<p>Strain the brandy mixture and discard the apples and spices. Pour the liquid&nbsp;into several glass bottles. Place an additional three cloves and one cinnamon stick in each bottle.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Recipe from&nbsp;https://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/apple-brandy/</sup></p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(44,'',41,1602673008,1602671445,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Learn more about apples','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,'17,19,20,22',2,'','',0,3,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(46,'',45,1602672065,1602671982,0,0,0,0,'',512,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'ingredients','Ingredients','','<table> 	<thead> 		<tr> 			<th scope=\"col\">Quantity</th> 			<th scope=\"col\">Products</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td>1/4 cup</td> 			<td>Butter, melted</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1</td> 			<td>Egg</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 cup</td> 			<td>Milk</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 cup</td> 			<td>Shredded tart apple</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 1/4 cups</td> 			<td>All-purpose flour</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 1/4 tsp</td> 			<td>Baking powder</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/4 tsp</td> 			<td>Ground cinnamon</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 tbsp</td> 			<td>White sugar</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(47,'',45,1618329914,1602672112,0,0,0,0,'',768,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Directions','','<p><strong>Step 1</strong></p>\r\n<p>Combine butter, milk,&nbsp;egg, and apple in a large bowl. Sift together flour, sugar,&nbsp;baking powder, and cinnamon in a separate bowl. Stir the flour mixture into the apple mixture until both mixtures are combined.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong></p>\r\n<p>Heat a lightly oiled frying pan or&nbsp;griddle over medium high heat. Pour the batter onto the pan or griddle, using about 1/4 cup for each pancake and bake until they are golden-brown. Serve the pancakes hot and enjoy!</p>\r\n<p><sup>Recipe from&nbsp;https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/23095/veronicas-apple-pancakes/</sup></p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(49,'',44,1602672809,1602672744,0,0,0,0,'',512,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'ingredients','Ingredients','','<table> 	<thead> 		<tr> 			<th scope=\"col\">Quantity</th> 			<th scope=\"col\">Product</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2 cup</td> 			<td>Oats</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2 cup</td> 			<td>Nonfat milk</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/4 cup</td> 			<td>Plain, nonfat yogurt</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2 cup</td> 			<td>Apple, chopped</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/8 tsp</td> 			<td>Ground cinnamon</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 tsp</td> 			<td>Honey</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 tsp</td> 			<td>Chia seeds</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(50,'',44,1607344843,1602672800,0,0,0,0,'',768,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Directions','','<p><strong>Step 1</strong></p>\r\n<p>Add all of the oats to a&nbsp;container of your choice and pour in low-fat yogurt and milk.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong></p>\r\n<p>Add in a layer of chopped apples, and top off with a drizzle of honey, cinnamon, and chia seeds.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 3</strong></p>\r\n<p>Place the container in your fridge and enjoy in the morning or a few hours later! Let it steep for at least 8 hours in a refrigerator 40Â° F or colder. Eat the Overnight Oat within 24 hours.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Recipe from&nbsp;https://www.quakeroats.com/cooking-and-recipes/apple-cinnamon-overnight-oats</sup></p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(51,'',44,1602675711,1602672907,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Learn more about apples','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,'26,21,22,19',2,'','',0,3,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(52,'',45,1602673024,1602672940,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Learn more about apples','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,'17,18,19,20',2,'','',0,3,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(58,'',20,1606616770,1602762068,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The apple tree is anually productive and grows moderately. Since it is susceptible to diseases like canker, mildew and scab, it is mostly grown in countries with a similar climate to that of England, such as the Netherlands and Belgium.&nbsp;In the UK it accounts for more than 50% of the acreage of dessert apples.</p>\r\n<p>The trees like well-aerated and wet soil as well as humid summers with low heat.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,1,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(61,'',20,1603183443,1602763365,0,0,0,0,'',32,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"colPos\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The Cox is the ideal apple to be eaten out of hand or sliced but also widely used in the production of cider, blended with other varieties.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Fun fact: </strong>If you shake a ripe Cox you should be hearing a rattling sound from the seeds as they are only loosely attached to the flesh.</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(62,'',17,1606831189,1602763427,0,0,0,0,'',1088,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','','','39,44,41,45',2,'','',0,2,1,0,'',0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,'','','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(63,'',18,1606831206,1602763434,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','','','41,45,53,54',2,'','',0,2,1,0,'',0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,'','','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(64,'',20,1606831239,1602763446,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','','','39,45,54,53',2,'','',0,2,1,0,'',0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,'','','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(66,'',21,1606616534,1602763582,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>Like most apples, Gala apples are available for sale almost all year due to controlled atmosphere and cold storage.</p>\r\n<p>In the northern hemisphere they are grown from May through September. The Gala apple available in Europe is mosty imported from Chile and New Zealand.<br /> Other countries like the UK, France, the USA, China, Argentinia and Brasil cultivate the trees commercially as well.</p>\r\n<p>The tree grows rather long and strong branches. Although the branches tend to break easily, the trees can grow a high number of apples at the same time.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,17,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,1,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(71,'',21,1606617983,1602766335,0,0,0,0,'',48,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>It is ideal snacking, cooking, salads and sauces.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> If you tend to have an allergic reaction&nbsp;to some apples, the Gala apple is known to be especially unsuitable.</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
