(74,'',17,1606733168,1602774458,0,0,0,0,'',1056,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Belle de Boskoop','','The apple cultivar Belle de Boskoop is - as its name suggests - originated in Boskoop, Netherlands. Starting as a chance seedling in 1856 and discovered by the pomologist Johannes Wilhelm Ottolander, it has been a wide-spread and popular cultivar since 1863.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(75,'',17,1606733180,1602774583,0,0,0,0,'',8,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"bodytext\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The apple with its many variants (red, yellow or green) is firm, fragrant, tart and can contain more than four times the vitamin C of â€œGolden Deliciousâ€ or â€œGranny Smithâ€.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
