(82,'',4,1606831348,1603101496,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_subpages','Homemade is always a good idea - try our simple recipes!','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,'',2,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(83,'',50,1606192172,1603109819,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"image\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'contentstage','Oops, something went wrong. Were you trying to compare apples and oranges again?','',NULL,0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(85,'',1,1606692616,1603126093,0,0,0,0,'',8,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"link\":null,\"image\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'mainteaser','Apples, apples, apples','','Apples are fascinating. You\'ve been eating them ever since you were young and you\'re probably still buying them regularly. You might even have an apple tree growing in your backyard. But we\'re pretty sure there still are some fun facts you don\'t know about this underestimated fruit.\r\n',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(86,'',2,1606729296,1603182430,0,0,0,0,'',1280,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Did you know that...','','<p>1. Apples have a long tradition in human history. Archaeologists have found evidence&nbsp;that people have been eating apples since 6,500 B.C.&nbsp;</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(88,'',18,1606733281,1603182831,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"bodytext\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Braeburn','','The apple cultivar Braeburn was first discovered as a chance seedling in 1952 by O. Moran from Waiwhero in the Moutere Hills in New Zealand. It was named after Braeburn Orchard near Motueka where it was first grown commercially.\r\n\r\nRecent research shows that the cultivar is the offspring of Delicious and Sturmer\'s Pippin, with Lady Hamilton as a sibling.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(89,'',18,1606733290,1603182999,0,0,0,0,'',32,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"bodytext\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The Braeburn apple has an orange-red vertical streaky look on a green/yellow background.\r\nIt is firm with a complex sweet-tart flavor which makes it especially popular in European countries.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(90,'',19,1606616854,1603183285,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Elstar','','The apple cultivar ElstarÂ was developed at the Institute for Plant breeding in WageningenÂ in the 1950s by crossing the apples Ingrid Marie and Golden Delicious.\r\n\r\nIt was first exported to America in 1972 and becameÂ popular in Europe very quickly. In 2012 the apple was the most cultivated variety in Germany.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(91,'',19,1606617614,1603183314,0,0,0,0,'',16,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The medium-sized apple with its mostly red skin and yellow showing is an aromatic, juicy and slightly sour but mostly sweet sort of apple. The flesh is white and has a crispy and soft texture.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(92,'',20,1606616811,1603183414,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Cox Orange','','The apple cultivar Cox\'s Orange Pippin (short British name is â€œCoxâ€) was first grown by Richard Cox, a retired horticulturist and brewer, in 1830 in Buckinghamshire, England.\r\n\r\nThe cultivar Ribston Pippin seems a likely candidate to be the cultivar\'s parentage, although that is yet to be confirmed.\r\n\r\nCharles Turner started selling the fruit in the 1850s and companies started growing them commercially in the 1860s.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(93,'',20,1603183931,1603183447,0,0,0,0,'',16,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The medium-sized apple with its red-orange colour and deep red mottle on yellow background is very popular due to its wonderful flavour.\r\nThe crisp and white-yellow flesh is very juicy, aromatic and subacid. Some say there are hints of anise and cherry which become less intense as the apple ages.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(94,'',21,1603183886,1603183783,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Gala','','The Gala apple trees resulted from a cross between a Kidd\'s Orange Red and a Golden Delicious and were first planted in New Zealand in the 1930s by James HuttonÂ Kidd.\r\n\r\nIn October 1974, an employee of Stark Bros Nursery received a US plant patent for the cultivar.Â \r\n\r\nThe cultivar has been one of the most popular in Switzerland and Germany as well as the UK and the USA.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(95,'',21,1603183804,1603183804,0,0,0,0,'',32,0,0,0,0,NULL,'',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The small to medium-sized Gala apple with its intense red colour on a golden-yellow background and vertical stripes is a sweet and aromatic apple with fine texture.Â ',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(96,'',22,1606616365,1603185374,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Gloster','','Gloster, aka Gloster 69, was first commercially sold in 1969.\r\nIt was first cultivated at the â€œObstbauversuchsanstalt Jork/Altes Landâ€ in Lower Saxony, Germany, in 1951.\r\nIt is usually only sold in stores with organic food.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(97,'',22,1603186534,1603185398,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The apple with its green-yellow and juicy flesh and slightly acid taste is known for its ruby red color.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(99,'',22,1603186506,1603186006,0,0,0,0,'',192,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The apple tree is a rather modest plant with no special requirements which is why it\'s ideal for backyard gardening: You will only need deep soil and enough water to grow it. The wood as well as the blossom of the tree are very frost-proof. The fruits are resistant to wind.</p>\r\n<p>Gloster apple trees are sensitive to fire and apple scab and grow from May to September. If stored for too long they tend to rot on the inside.</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(100,'',23,1603189062,1603189062,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Golden Delicious','','The Golden Delicious cultivar is a chance seedling and assumed to be a hybrid of Golden Reinette and Grimes Golden. The original tree was first found on a farm in West Virginia, USA. The farmer Anderson Mullins sold the tree and propagation rights to Stark Brothers Nurseries. The company then sold the apple commercially in 1914 - accompanied by their Red Delicious.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(101,'',23,1603189236,1603189127,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The large apple with its green-yellowish skin is famous for its very sweet taste and therefore one of the 15 most popular cultivars in the United States.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(102,'',23,1606618023,1603189175,0,0,0,0,'',192,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>It is ideal for apple sauce, apple butter and salads.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> If you tend to have an allergic reaction&nbsp;to some apples, you should avoid a&nbsp;Golden Delicious.</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(103,'',23,1606616196,1603189818,0,0,0,0,'',224,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The Golden Delicious is rather tolerant to a great number of soil and climates, though it is not very frost resistant. The trees grow best on humid soil in warm climates with dry and sunny summers and is harvested from fall through winter.</p>\r\n<p>If kept at ideal conditions the apples can be stored until the next harvest.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> In order to prevent the apples from turning wrinkled&nbsp;they are usually waxed before storage.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,17,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
