(111,'',53,1603203608,1603203237,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Apple Cucumber Smoothie','','It\'s green, it\'s healthy, it\'s low in calories and it\'s so good! Our Apple cucumber Smoothie is the perfect choice if you want to stay healthy.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(112,'',53,1603203394,1603203394,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'',0,0,0,0,'ingredients','Ingredients','','<table> 	<thead> 		<tr> 			<th scope=\"col\">Quantity</th> 			<th scope=\"col\">Product</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td>3/4 cup</td> 			<td>Coconut water or water</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>2</td> 			<td>Green apples, cored and quartered</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/4&nbsp;</td> 			<td>English cucumber, chopped</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2 bunch</td> 			<td>Flat leaf parsley, leaves only, chopped</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 slice piece</td> 			<td>Ginger, 1 inch thick</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1&nbsp;</td> 			<td>Medium lemon, peeled and seeded</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 cup</td> 			<td>Ice cubes</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(113,'',53,1607345104,1603203516,0,0,0,0,'',192,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Directions','','<p><strong>Step 1</strong></p>\r\n<p>Put all the ingredients in a high-quality blender, starting with the liquids. Blend until all ingredients&nbsp;are smooth.<br /> <strong>Alternative</strong>: If you don\'t like it pulpy, run the mixture through a mesh sieve.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong></p>\r\n<p>Pour the smoothie into 2 glasses with ice.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 3</strong></p>\r\n<p>Enjoy!</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source:&nbsp;https://www.skinnytaste.com/green-apple-lemon-cucumber-ginger-smoothie/</sup></p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(114,'',54,1603203919,1603203919,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Apple Cinnamon Tea','','Get cozy on your sofa and have a nice cup of a homemade Apple Cinnamon tea. It\'s the perfect choice for cold winter days!',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(115,'',54,1606751166,1603203999,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'ingredients','Ingredients','','<table> 	<thead> 		<tr> 			<th scope=\"col\">Quantity</th> 			<th scope=\"col\">Product</th> 		</tr> 	</thead> 	<tbody> 		<tr> 			<td>3 cups</td> 			<td>Water</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2</td> 			<td>Apple</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 inch</td> 			<td>Cinnamon</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2 inch</td> 			<td>Ginger piece</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1 tbsp</td> 			<td>Lemon juice</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>4</td> 			<td>Whole peppercorns</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td>1/2 tsp</td> 			<td>Tea powder</td> 		</tr> 		<tr> 			<td></td> 			<td>Honey or Sugar</td> 		</tr> 	</tbody> </table>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(116,'',54,1607345161,1603204168,0,0,0,0,'',192,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Directions','','<p><strong>Step 1</strong></p>\r\n<p>Place all the ingredients (except sugar/honey&nbsp;and apples) into a deep pot.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 2</strong></p>\r\n<p>Boil until it reduces to 2 cups.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 3</strong></p>\r\n<p>While the tea is boiling, wash, peel and mince the apple.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 4</strong></p>\r\n<p>Take the pot off the stove and add the apple pieces to it.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 5</strong></p>\r\n<p>Cover the pot with a lid, letting it sit for 5 minutes.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Step 6</strong></p>\r\n<p>Strain the apple tea, add sugar or honey and enjoy!</p>\r\n<p><sup>Recipe from&nbsp;https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/apple-tea-recipe-apple-cinnamon-tea-best-winter-tea-recipe/</sup></p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(117,'',4,1606744194,1603204512,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"header\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Easy recipes for apple lovers','','Don\'t you just love the idea of breakfast-in-bed with delicious Apple Pancakes?Â Or the smell of a freshly-baked Apple Pie for your afternoon coffee break?\r\n\r\nApples are easy to get throughout the year and can be turned into the most delicious meals and drinks.\r\nHere are some simple ideas for your next cooking session!',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(118,'',3,1606618176,1603204822,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','How do you like them apples?','','No matter how hard you try, you can\'t compare apples and oranges. That is as sure as God made little green apples.\r\n\r\nBut there are amazing things you probably didn\'t know about this kind of fruit.\r\n\r\nWhy don\'t you dive into the world of apples with us?',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(119,'',22,1606831268,1603204941,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','','','44,53,41,45',2,'','',0,2,1,0,'',0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,'','','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(120,'',23,1606831283,1603204976,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','','','41,44,39,53',2,'','',0,2,1,0,'',0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,'','','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(121,'',24,1606831302,1603204990,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','','','53,41,44,39',2,'','',0,2,1,0,'',0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,'','','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(122,'',2,1607505992,1603205118,0,0,0,0,'',1152,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','10 astonishing things you certainly don\'t know about apples','','Most people eat them, most people love them. But only few of us know a lot about the fruit called apple.\r\nHere are some facts that are probably new to you!',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(123,'',24,1606615923,1603206141,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Granny Smith','','The Granny Smith is a chance seedling and was first grown in Australia in 1868 by Maria Ann Smith. It is most likely a hybrid of Malus pumila as the polleniser and Malus sylvestris.\r\nFun fact: There is a festival called the â€œGranny Smith Festivalâ€ that takes place in Eastwood (a suburb of Sydney) every October with about 60,000 people! ',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(124,'',24,1606615966,1603206332,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The hard apple with its light green skin and juicy, crisp flesh is famous for its acidic and tart flavour. The acidic flavour is not caused by a lack of sugar, though, but by a high level of fruit acid. \r\nWhen overripe the green turns yellow.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(125,'',24,1603206397,1603206397,0,0,0,0,'',96,0,0,0,0,NULL,'',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','It remains firm even when baked which makes it a popular choice for pies. In 2019 it was reported the third most popular apple in America.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(126,'',24,1606618049,1603206580,0,0,0,0,'',112,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The fruit grows best in hot climates and takes a long time to fully grow.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> If you tend to have an allergic reaction&nbsp;to some apples, the Granny Smith is not a good choice.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(127,'',25,1603272282,1603270574,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Jonagold','','The cultivar Jonagold (also known as Jonagored or Red Prince) was developed at the New York State Agricultural Experiment Station of Cornell University\'s College of Agriculture and Life Sciences in 1943 and was sold commercially in 1968. It is a cross between Jonathan and Golden Delicious and is one of the six most planted cultivars worldwide.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(128,'',25,1606615876,1603270831,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The aromatic and juicy fruit with its sweet-sour taste is famous for its fluffily crisp flesh. The skin can be golden-red or sometimes even be fully red or fully green.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(129,'',25,1603273024,1603271366,0,0,0,0,'',192,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The cultivar is mostly grown in Northern and Eastern Europe and prefers warm climates and deep, fertile soil to grow the trees. They are not as sensitive to frost, mildew or apple scab as other cultivars.</p>\r\n<p>Jonagold apples can be stored easily.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(130,'',25,1603271560,1603271512,0,0,0,0,'',160,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>Jonagold Apples are ideal to be eaten fresh as a snack, for salads, juice, ciders or baking.</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(131,'',25,1606831318,1603271545,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,'39,41,45,54',2,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(132,'',26,1606615530,1603271870,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','Pink Lady','','The cultivar Pink Lady, originally known as Cripps Pink, was first developed by the Australian scientist John Cripps in 1973 and is a hybrid between the cultivars Lady Williams and Golden Delicious. It was introduced to the market in 1986.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(133,'',26,1603271935,1603271879,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'lead','','','The Cripps Pink is famous for its purple-red skin on yellow-green background. The fruit is crisp and tart, rather sweet and less juicy than other cultivars.',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(134,'',26,1603273039,1603272230,0,0,0,0,'',192,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The cultivar is known for its long growing period as it only develops its red colour by the end of the season. It only fully ripens in ideal climates which is why it is mostly grown in countries like France, Spain, Chile, South Africa or Australia.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The cultivar is very sensitive to mildew.</p>\r\n<p>Since the apples can be stored easily they are available in stores all year.</p>\r\n<p><sup>Source: wikipedia.org</sup></p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,17,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(135,'',26,1606618087,1603272491,0,0,0,0,'',160,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>The apple is the perfect choice for eating out of the hand, as well as for baking.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Side note:</strong> If you tend to have an allergic reaction&nbsp;to some apples, you should avoid&nbsp;a Pink Lady.&nbsp;</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(136,'',26,1606831330,1603272559,0,0,0,0,'',64,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"pages\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"accessibility_title\":null,\"accessibility_bypass\":null,\"accessibility_bypass_text\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'menu_pages','Easy recipes for apple lovers','',NULL,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,'53,44,39,54',2,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(138,'',52,1606835968,1603359737,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"link\":null,\"linklabel\":null,\"linkconfig\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'keyvisual','3 shocking secrets about apples','','These apple secrets are only available to users who are logged in. If you can see this page, you must be logged in. \r\nBeing able to restrict access to pages or content for logged-in users is a default feature of TYPO3. Isn\'t that cool?\r\n\r\nNow that you\'re logged in, go back to the Fun Facts page and see what\'s new.',0,0,0,0,1,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,1,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(139,'',52,1606193903,1603360888,0,0,0,0,'',128,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Did you know that...','','<ol> 	<li>The apple pie now known as the typical American Apple pie is not an American invention.&nbsp;In fact, it was originally invented in&nbsp;England in the 1300\'s.</li> 	<li>The pie we know and love wasn\'t supposed to be eaten with a crust. Back in the 1300\'s, they didn\'t have a&nbsp;tin to hold the pie so inventive cooks created a mixture&nbsp;made of lard, water and flour to act as a temporary container for the pie. Today\'s version might not be what was originally intended, but we all know the crust is what makes the apple pie so delicious.&nbsp;</li> 	<li>There are people who are afraid of eating apples, and some who suffer from a fear of apples in general. This phobia is called Malusdomesticaphobia.&nbsp;</li> </ol>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(140,'',2,1607422443,1603361235,0,0,0,0,'1',64,1,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','Great, you\'re logged in!','','<p>This content only displays for people who have logged in to the frontend. Here is a treat for you. Sit back, relax and enjoy the comedy gold of Annoying Orange.</p>\r\n<p>You can control visibility of content at the page level, or for&nbsp;individual pieces of content like this. In the backend, when you edit content, go to the <strong>Access </strong>tab and you can decide which usergroups will be able to see the&nbsp;content. It\'s just so easy with TYPO3!</p>',0,0,0,1,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,2,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(141,'',1,1607010462,1603791569,0,0,0,0,'',4,1,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'resetbanner','Welcome to our TYPO3 Demo website','','As you might notice: None of us is a pomologist, and we know just as much as Wikipedia knows about apples.\r\nThis website is not about apples, it\'s all about showcasing TYPO3 CMS. Because that is what we know best.\r\nThis website gives you a deeper look at how TYPO3 works. Why don\'t you login to the backend and try out what you can do? \r\nFeel free to edit or delete content - don\'t worry about breaking things. We reset the system 30 minutes after someone has logged in.\r\n',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,22,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(142,'',2,1606691772,1603866748,0,0,0,0,'',1408,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>2. For the health-conscious: An apple only has about 80 calories, is free from cholesterol, fat&nbsp;and sodium;&nbsp;and is also a wonderful source of fiber.</p>\r\n<p>So, no need to feel bad if you\'re craving another apple!</p>\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(143,'',2,1606691753,1603866769,0,0,0,0,'',1472,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>3. Scientists who specialize&nbsp;in the branch of botany concerned with&nbsp;fruit&nbsp;cultivation&nbsp;are called â€œpomologistsâ€. The science is called â€œpomologyâ€ (in Latin&nbsp;â€œpomumâ€ means fruit).<br /> &nbsp;</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(144,'',2,1606691802,1603866803,0,0,0,0,'',1504,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>4. Most apples are still picked by hand, even to the present day. Not by robots or machines. By actual human beings.</p>\r\n<p>Crazy, right?</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(145,'',2,1606691854,1603866822,0,0,0,0,'',1520,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>5. Have you ever wondered why apples float? It\'s because they are 25% air!</p>\r\n<p>There is&nbsp;a popular and fun game called â€œApple bobbingâ€ that relies on floating apples. Just fill a tub or a basin with water, put in some apples and try to get them out using nothing but your mouth. Simple, but so much fun!</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(146,'',2,1606691911,1603866839,0,0,0,0,'',1528,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>6. When&nbsp;stored at room temperature, apples ripen up to 10 times faster than if they were refrigerated.</p>\r\n<p>If you don\'t want to eat or use them any time soon, just put them somewhere cool (like the basement) or in your fridge.</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(147,'',2,1606691957,1603866857,0,0,0,0,'',1532,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>7. An average apple tree produces 100 - 300 pounds of fruit per year. Apple trees live between 50 - 75 years, so you can make&nbsp;quite a number of apple pies from just one tree. Better start baking right now...</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(148,'',2,1606692330,1603866872,0,0,0,0,'',1534,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>8. George Washington loved pruning his apple trees as a hobby.&nbsp;He added orchards to the outlying farms of his historic home, Mount Vernon, growing&nbsp;apples, pears, cherries, peaches, and apricots.</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(149,'',2,1604498017,1603866885,0,0,0,0,'',1535,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"image\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>9. Apple juice was one of the first drugs to serve as antidepressants.</p>\r\n<p>Well, we never feel worse after having a glass of apple juice...</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(150,'',2,1616145950,1603866905,0,0,0,0,'',1791,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":null,\"colPos\":null,\"header\":null,\"header_layout\":null,\"bodytext\":null,\"assets\":null,\"imageorient\":null,\"sys_language_uid\":null,\"hidden\":null,\"starttime\":null,\"endtime\":null,\"fe_group\":null,\"editlock\":null,\"rowDescription\":null}',0,0,0,0,'textmedia','','','<p>10. The first American to orbit Earth was John Glenn. For his initial space flight he took squeezable tubes of pureed applesauce with him.</p>\r\n<p>This guy just knew what\'s good!</p>',0,0,0,1,1,0,18,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,0,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
(151,'',56,1643192179,1603967603,0,0,0,0,'',256,0,0,0,0,NULL,'{\"CType\":\"\",\"colPos\":\"\",\"header\":\"\",\"header_layout\":\"\",\"bodytext\":\"\",\"sys_language_uid\":\"\",\"hidden\":\"\",\"starttime\":\"\",\"endtime\":\"\",\"fe_group\":\"\",\"editlock\":\"\",\"rowDescription\":\"\"}',0,0,0,0,'faqlist','Frequently Asked Questions','','<p>We get endless questions about apples every day. It seems like we\'ll never get to the core of what makes apples so interesting! (To be fair, we are exaggerating a little here...)</p>\r\n<p>Try&nbsp;adding your own question and answer to this page by <a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3\">logging in with the FAQ Editor</a> usergroup.&nbsp;As an FAQ editor, you can go straight to the <a href=\"https://demo.typo3.org/typo3/module/web/faq\">FAQ module</a> in the backend to edit, delete and hide the FAQs for this page.</p>\r\n<p>TYPO3 makes it easy to build custom backend modules that are&nbsp;exactly suited to specific needs - like the FAQ module used to build this page.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Administrators can restrict an editor\'s access to a particular module,&nbsp;which makes it really great for editors who only need to edit this specific part of the website.&nbsp;</p>',0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'','default',0,'','',NULL,NULL,0,'','',0,1,1,0,NULL,0,'','','',0,0,0,NULL,NULL,'','',NULL,124,0,0,0,0,'','',''),
