(10,36,1052,0,1606614018,1603981402,0,0,0,'{\"question\":null,\"answer\":null}',0,0,NULL,'Can you compare apples to oranges?','<p>Yes, but there is only one man who could ever do it: Chuck Norris.</p>'),
(11,36,1048,0,1606614239,1603982121,0,0,0,'{\"question\":null,\"answer\":null}',0,0,NULL,'What kind of apple did Eve use to tempt Adam?','<p>Adam and Eve covered themselves with fig leaves after eating the fruit, so scientists assume it was more likely to be a fig than an apple.</p>\r\n<p>Scientists supporting the â€œfig theoryâ€&nbsp;also suppose that there has been an error in translation, because&nbsp;the Latin word â€œmalusâ€&nbsp;can be translated as â€œevilâ€&nbsp;but also as â€œapple treeâ€. The original text uses the word â€œPeriâ€&nbsp;which simply&nbsp;means â€œfruitâ€.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Nobody really knows for sure, but the fruit was most likely <u>not</u> the apple we know today.</p>'),
(12,36,1152,0,1606612485,1603982520,0,0,0,'{\"question\":null,\"answer\":null}',0,0,NULL,'Why did Steve Jobs name his company â€œAppleâ€?','<p>Walter Isaacson\'s&nbsp;biography, \"<a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/11084145-steve-jobs\" target=\"_blank\">Steve Jobs</a>\", reveals it was during one of his fruitarian diets when he had just come back from visiting an apple farm.&nbsp;<br /> Jobs thought the name â€œAppleâ€&nbsp;sounded â€œfun, spirited and not intimidatingâ€. So, there you go!</p>\r\n\r\n'),
(13,36,1040,0,1606752275,1603982725,0,0,0,'{\"question\":null,\"answer\":null}',0,0,NULL,'Do apples really keep the doctor away?','<p>A study published by The American Journal of Clinical Nutrition (December&nbsp;2019) states that eating two apples a day lowers serum cholesterol and improves cardiometabolic biomarkers in mildly hypercholesterolemic adults (<a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/ajcn/article/111/2/307/5675325\">read more</a>).<br /> Eating apples has beneficial effects on lipid metabolism and other markers of cardiovascular disease.</p>\r\n<p>This proves the old saying true, so have you eaten yours today?</p>'),
(14,36,1056,0,1606612628,1603982969,0,0,0,'{\"question\":null,\"answer\":null}',0,0,NULL,'What is the best way to store apples at home?','<p>If you\'re planning on eating your apples within the next few days, keep them in the refrigerator. If you would like to store them for a longer period of time, you should choose a cool and dark room with high humidity. The basement in your house is usually an ideal place.</p>'),
(15,36,8,0,1606614720,1603983089,0,0,0,'{\"question\":null,\"answer\":null}',0,0,NULL,'What do apples have in common with TYPO3?','<p>They are both delightful and make your day sweeter.</p>'),
(17,36,524,15,1606751985,1606751953,0,1,15,'{\"question\":\"What do apples have in common with TYPO3?\",\"answer\":\"<p>They are both delightful and make your day sweeter.<\\/p>\",\"t3_origuid\":0,\"sys_language_uid\":0,\"l10n_parent\":0,\"disabled\":0,\"l10n_source\":0}',0,15,NULL,'Was haben Ã„pfel und TYPO3 gemeinsam?','<p>Sie sind beide groÃŸartig und versÃ¼ÃŸen deinen Tag!</p>'),
(18,36,526,13,1613475156,1606751989,0,1,13,'{\"question\":\"Do apples really keep the doctor away?\",\"answer\":\"<p>A study published by The American Journal of Clinical Nutrition (December&nbsp;2019) states that eating two apples a day lowers serum cholesterol and improves cardiometabolic biomarkers in mildly hypercholesterolemic adults (<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/academic.oup.com\\/ajcn\\/article\\/111\\/2\\/307\\/5675325\\\">read more<\\/a>).<br \\/> Eating apples has beneficial effects on lipid metabolism and other markers of cardiovascular disease.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>This proves the old saying true, so have you eaten yours today?<\\/p>\",\"t3_origuid\":0,\"sys_language_uid\":0,\"l10n_parent\":0,\"disabled\":0,\"l10n_source\":0}',0,13,NULL,'Halten Ã„pfel mich wirklich gesund (â€œAn apple a day...â€)','<p>Eine Studie von The American Journal of Clinical Nutrition (Dezember 2019) fand heraus, dass der Verzehr von zwei Ã„pfeln pro Tag den Cholesterinspiegel senkt und die&nbsp;kardiometabolischen Biomarker bei leicht hypercholesterinÃ¤mischen Erwachsenen verbessert (<a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/ajcn/article/111/2/307/5675325\">Mehr Infos</a>).<br /> Der Verzehr von Ã„pfeln hat auÃŸerdem positive Effekte auf den Fettstoffwechsel und andere Marker kardiovaskulÃ¤rer Krankheiten.<br /> <br /> Das beweist, dass das alte Sprichwort doch einen Funken Wahrheit beinhaltet.&nbsp;Hast du deine Ã„pfel heute schon gegessen?</p>'),
(19,36,527,11,1606752497,1606752280,0,1,11,'{\"question\":\"What kind of apple did Eve use to tempt Adam?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Adam and Eve covered themselves with fig leaves after eating the fruit, so scientists assume it was more likely to be a fig than an apple.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>Scientists supporting the \\u201cfig theory\\u201d&nbsp;also suppose that there has been an error in translation, because&nbsp;the Latin word \\u201cmalus\\u201d&nbsp;can be translated as \\u201cevil\\u201d&nbsp;but also as \\u201capple tree\\u201d. The original text uses the word \\u201cPeri\\u201d&nbsp;which simply&nbsp;means \\u201cfruit\\u201d.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>Nobody really knows for sure, but the fruit was most likely <u>not<\\/u> the apple we know today.<\\/p>\",\"t3_origuid\":0,\"sys_language_uid\":0,\"l10n_parent\":0,\"disabled\":0,\"l10n_source\":0}',0,11,NULL,'Welche Apfelsorte nutzte Eva, um Adam zu verfÃ¼hren?','<p>Adam und Eva bedeckten sich mit FeigenblÃ¤ttern, nachdem sie die verbotene Frucht gegessen hatten. Aus diesem Grund vermuten Wissenschaftler, dass es sich vielmehr um eine Feige handelte als um einen Apfel.</p>\r\n<p>Wissenschaftler, die die \"Feigen-Theorie\" vertreten, vermuten auÃŸerdem, dass es sich um einen Ãœbersetzungsfehler handelt: Im Lateinischen bedeutet das Wort â€œmalusâ€ sowohl â€œbÃ¶seâ€ als auch â€œApfelbaumâ€. Im Originaltext wird hier jedoch das Wort â€œPeriâ€ verwendet, das schlichtweg â€œFruchtâ€ bedeutet.</p>\r\n<p>Keiner weiÃŸ es genau, aber die Frucht war mit hoher wahrscheinlich <u>nicht</u> der Apfel, den wir heute kennen.</p>'),
(20,36,783,10,1606752538,1606752503,0,1,10,'{\"question\":\"Can you compare apples to oranges?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Yes, but there is only one man who could ever do it: Chuck Norris.<\\/p>\",\"t3_origuid\":0,\"sys_language_uid\":0,\"l10n_parent\":0,\"disabled\":0,\"l10n_source\":0}',0,10,NULL,'Kann man Ã„pfeln mit Birnen vergleichen?','<p>Ja, aber dazu ist nur genau ein Mann im Stande: Chuck Norris.</p>'),
(21,36,911,14,1606752672,1606752608,0,1,14,'{\"question\":\"What is the best way to store apples at home?\",\"answer\":\"<p>If you\'re planning on eating your apples within the next few days, keep them in the refrigerator. If you would like to store them for a longer period of time, you should choose a cool and dark room with high humidity. The basement in your house is usually an ideal place.<\\/p>\",\"t3_origuid\":0,\"sys_language_uid\":0,\"l10n_parent\":0,\"disabled\":0,\"l10n_source\":0}',0,14,NULL,'Wie lagert man Ã„pfel am besten zu Hause?','<p>Wenn Du die Ã„pfel in den nÃ¤chsten Tagen essen mÃ¶chtest, lagere sie am besten im KÃ¼hlschrank.&nbsp;<br /> Wenn Du sie fÃ¼r eine lÃ¤ngere Zeit lagern willst, solltest Du einen kÃ¼hlen und dunklen Ort wÃ¤hlen mit hoher Luftfeuchtigkeit. Der Keller im Haus ist in der Regel ein idealer Ort dafÃ¼r.</p>'),
(22,36,975,12,1606753108,1606752678,0,1,12,'{\"question\":\"Why did Steve Jobs name his company \\u201cApple\\u201d?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Walter Isaacson\'s&nbsp;biography, \\\"<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.goodreads.com\\/book\\/show\\/11084145-steve-jobs\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Steve Jobs<\\/a>\\\", reveals it was during one of his fruitarian diets when he had just come back from visiting an apple farm.&nbsp;<br \\/> Jobs thought the name \\u201cApple\\u201d&nbsp;sounded \\u201cfun, spirited and not intimidating\\u201d. So, there you go!<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\"t3_origuid\":0,\"sys_language_uid\":0,\"l10n_parent\":0,\"disabled\":0,\"l10n_source\":0}',0,12,NULL,'Warum nannte Steve Jobs seine Firma â€œAppleâ€?','<p>Walter Isaacson beschreibt in der Biografie&nbsp;â€œSteve Jobsâ€, dass der Name nach einer Frutarier-DiÃ¤t des GrÃ¼nders entstanden ist, nachdem er einige Zeit&nbsp;auf einer Apfelfarm verbracht hatte.<br /> Jobs fand, dass der Name â€œAppleâ€ â€œspaÃŸig, temperamentvoll und nicht einschÃ¼chterndâ€ klingt.&nbsp;<br /> Klingt gut, oder?</p>'),
